Subject: [PATCH 2/4] crypto: sun4i-ss: expose algorithms to userspace

Clear CRYPTO_ALG_KERN_DRIVER_ONLY from each algorithm immediately before
registration. This makes the driver's algorithms available through AF_ALG for
hardware validation while keeping the change independent of the V821 DMA path.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [local hardware validation support]

---
--- a/drivers/crypto/allwinner/sun4i-ss/sun4i-ss-core.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/allwinner/sun4i-ss/sun4i-ss-core.c
@@ -435,5 +435,15 @@
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(ss_algs); i++) {
 		ss_algs[i].ss = ss;
+		switch (ss_algs[i].type) {
+		case CRYPTO_ALG_TYPE_SKCIPHER:
+			ss_algs[i].alg.crypto.base.cra_flags &=
+				~CRYPTO_ALG_KERN_DRIVER_ONLY;
+			break;
+		case CRYPTO_ALG_TYPE_AHASH:
+			ss_algs[i].alg.hash.halg.base.cra_flags &=
+				~CRYPTO_ALG_KERN_DRIVER_ONLY;
+			break;
+		}
 		switch (ss_algs[i].type) {
 		case CRYPTO_ALG_TYPE_SKCIPHER:
 			err = crypto_register_skcipher(&ss_algs[i].alg.crypto);
-- 
